[{:db/id "a4c875e9-9286-5098-a619-c210f8e79f4c" :answer/id #uuid "a4c875e9-9286-5098-a619-c210f8e79f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i-2 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "78649c28-3f6b-5c90-bcdf-d6aae7f64441" :answer/id #uuid "78649c28-3f6b-5c90-bcdf-d6aae7f64441" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 \\cos{(1 )}\\,i-8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,j" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "32b0c782-0ae8-567b-8b5c-f140f678674a" :answer/id #uuid "32b0c782-0ae8-567b-8b5c-f140f678674a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i+2 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "10175385-4f52-58f4-a77c-fcc932f5b130" :answer/id #uuid "10175385-4f52-58f4-a77c-fcc932f5b130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i+2 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4a6a4fac-5734-5eb0-9ed6-a928757ce0a9" :answer/id #uuid "4a6a4fac-5734-5eb0-9ed6-a928757ce0a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i-6 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "502f7d26-3a3c-5b78-942c-f5b26d010ea8" :answer-field/id #uuid "502f7d26-3a3c-5b78-942c-f5b26d010ea8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["a4c875e9-9286-5098-a619-c210f8e79f4c" "78649c28-3f6b-5c90-bcdf-d6aae7f64441" "32b0c782-0ae8-567b-8b5c-f140f678674a" "10175385-4f52-58f4-a77c-fcc932f5b130" "4a6a4fac-5734-5eb0-9ed6-a928757ce0a9"] :answer-field/correct "32b0c782-0ae8-567b-8b5c-f140f678674a" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "48a5b0a5-ecb9-5e4e-bbb7-138d96fc81cd" :question/id #uuid "48a5b0a5-ecb9-5e4e-bbb7-138d96fc81cd" :question/problem "In what direction does the function $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ decrease most rapidly at the point $(1,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y)$ decreases most rapidly in the direction opposite to that of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y-4y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\  & =(4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)\\text{ }i+(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\text{ }j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =(4\\cdot (1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))+4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(1))\\text{ }i+(2(1)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1))\\text{ }j \\\\  & =8 \\sin{(1 )}\\text{ }i-2 \\cos{(1 )}\\text{ }j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function decreases most rapidly in the direction of $-8 \\sin{(1 )}\\,i+2 \\cos{(1 )}\\,j.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["502f7d26-3a3c-5b78-942c-f5b26d010ea8"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "4db28b1e-53e6-5ed7-97fe-dfc2547a1e58" :answer/id #uuid "4db28b1e-53e6-5ed7-97fe-dfc2547a1e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{2}{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fab2ca73-8b3b-5efe-aa63-5406ad5f0f2d" :answer/id #uuid "fab2ca73-8b3b-5efe-aa63-5406ad5f0f2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "777d568e-614a-5fe8-972d-c790f3d57fd7" :answer/id #uuid "777d568e-614a-5fe8-972d-c790f3d57fd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e7deec0f-97e7-5173-bce8-8cd81ee664db" :answer/id #uuid "e7deec0f-97e7-5173-bce8-8cd81ee664db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fcf2d532-6987-5e82-abef-4a6d41f98545" :answer/id #uuid "fcf2d532-6987-5e82-abef-4a6d41f98545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ce582fa9-bf54-5250-b517-f810eb01ce45" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce582fa9-bf54-5250-b517-f810eb01ce45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["4db28b1e-53e6-5ed7-97fe-dfc2547a1e58" "fab2ca73-8b3b-5efe-aa63-5406ad5f0f2d" "777d568e-614a-5fe8-972d-c790f3d57fd7" "e7deec0f-97e7-5173-bce8-8cd81ee664db" "fcf2d532-6987-5e82-abef-4a6d41f98545"] :answer-field/correct "fcf2d532-6987-5e82-abef-4a6d41f98545" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a6e0bfcc-2db2-5134-b63f-ed16edd03447" :question/id #uuid "a6e0bfcc-2db2-5134-b63f-ed16edd03447" :question/problem "In what unit direction does the function $f(x,y,z)=\\ln (x^{2}y^{1}z^{6})$ increase most rapidly at the point $(1,1,3)$?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (x^{2}y^{1}z^{6})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln (x^{2}y^{1}z^{6})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\ln (x^{2}y^{1}z^{6}))⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{1}{x^{2}y^{1}z^{6}}\\cdot 2x^{1}y^{1}z^{6},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{2}y^{1}z^{6}}\\cdot x^{2}y^{0}z^{6},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{2}y^{1}z^{6}}\\cdot 6x^{2}y^{1}z^{5}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{2}{x},\\,\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{6}{z}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(1,1,3) & =⟨\\frac{2}{1},\\,\\frac{1}{1},\\,\\frac{6}{3}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{∇f(1,1,3)}{‖∇f(1,1,3)‖} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(2)^{2}}}⟨2,\\,1,\\,2⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the unit direction of $⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["ce582fa9-bf54-5250-b517-f810eb01ce45"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "9dc035af-ed1b-551a-8b01-10f5d3b91125" :answer/id #uuid "9dc035af-ed1b-551a-8b01-10f5d3b91125" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,-\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2880b2e8-4f16-5d70-bb12-a638f2d32836" :answer/id #uuid "2880b2e8-4f16-5d70-bb12-a638f2d32836" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,\\,2,\\,4⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "65dd24b1-670c-595e-ac35-85b55310a28c" :answer/id #uuid "65dd24b1-670c-595e-ac35-85b55310a28c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{21},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{21}}{21},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{21}}{21}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4e8a0998-482a-549c-b11c-b4cdf16a0a4e" :answer/id #uuid "4e8a0998-482a-549c-b11c-b4cdf16a0a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3}{29},\\,\\frac{2}{29},\\,\\frac{4}{29}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "eaec32c4-2c02-5eff-a1fa-2a8399d25d1c" :answer/id #uuid "eaec32c4-2c02-5eff-a1fa-2a8399d25d1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dfa4117b-a299-576c-9a40-7e9a99268421" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfa4117b-a299-576c-9a40-7e9a99268421" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["9dc035af-ed1b-551a-8b01-10f5d3b91125" "2880b2e8-4f16-5d70-bb12-a638f2d32836" "65dd24b1-670c-595e-ac35-85b55310a28c" "4e8a0998-482a-549c-b11c-b4cdf16a0a4e" "eaec32c4-2c02-5eff-a1fa-2a8399d25d1c"] :answer-field/correct "eaec32c4-2c02-5eff-a1fa-2a8399d25d1c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "6d226b9a-26b3-5e84-bd16-a03937995368" :question/id #uuid "6d226b9a-26b3-5e84-bd16-a03937995368" :question/problem "In what unit direction does the function $f(x,y,z)=\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})$ increase most rapidly at the point $(1,1,1)$?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}))⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 3x^{2}y^{2}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 2x^{3}y^{1}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 4x^{3}y^{2}z^{3}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{3}{x},\\,\\frac{2}{y},\\,\\frac{4}{z}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(1,1,1) & =⟨\\frac{3}{1},\\,\\frac{2}{1},\\,\\frac{4}{1}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{∇f(1,1,1)}{‖∇f(1,1,1)‖} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(4)^{2}}}⟨3,\\,2,\\,4⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the unit direction of $⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["dfa4117b-a299-576c-9a40-7e9a99268421"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "24f1dbef-5fc8-59db-bec0-0a9c8a04f080" :answer/id #uuid "24f1dbef-5fc8-59db-bec0-0a9c8a04f080" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2 \\sqrt{26}}{13},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{26},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{26}}{26}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8267fe08-c361-5516-bb08-f2287927df19" :answer/id #uuid "8267fe08-c361-5516-bb08-f2287927df19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{11},\\,-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{11}}{11}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e89ef417-189c-5198-b034-c7b157620d77" :answer/id #uuid "e89ef417-189c-5198-b034-c7b157620d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{6}{13},\\,-\\frac{3}{26},\\,-\\frac{9}{26}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "13eb88b0-c538-59f5-a87f-9f0c62715e7c" :answer/id #uuid "13eb88b0-c538-59f5-a87f-9f0c62715e7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{3},\\,-\\frac{1}{3},\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c20caa2a-1e3e-5e4e-8c04-1a085e20bfe5" :answer/id #uuid "c20caa2a-1e3e-5e4e-8c04-1a085e20bfe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{26}}{13},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{26},\\,-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{26}}{26}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "13f6643a-75d9-50a2-a3fb-88100e3589a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "13f6643a-75d9-50a2-a3fb-88100e3589a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["24f1dbef-5fc8-59db-bec0-0a9c8a04f080" "8267fe08-c361-5516-bb08-f2287927df19" "e89ef417-189c-5198-b034-c7b157620d77" "13eb88b0-c538-59f5-a87f-9f0c62715e7c" "c20caa2a-1e3e-5e4e-8c04-1a085e20bfe5"] :answer-field/correct "c20caa2a-1e3e-5e4e-8c04-1a085e20bfe5" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b1292b8d-2b01-5533-896d-f2505b0485b1" :question/id #uuid "b1292b8d-2b01-5533-896d-f2505b0485b1" :question/problem "In what unit direction does the function $f(x,y,z)=\\ln (x^{4}y^{1}z^{3})$ decrease most rapidly at the point $(3,3,3)$?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ decreases most rapidly in the direction opposite to that of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(3,3,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (x^{4}y^{1}z^{3})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln (x^{4}y^{1}z^{3})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\ln (x^{4}y^{1}z^{3}))⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{1}{x^{4}y^{1}z^{3}}\\cdot 4x^{3}y^{1}z^{3},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{4}y^{1}z^{3}}\\cdot x^{4}y^{0}z^{3},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{4}y^{1}z^{3}}\\cdot 3x^{4}y^{1}z^{2}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{4}{x},\\,\\frac{1}{y},\\,\\frac{3}{z}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(3,3,3) & =⟨\\frac{4}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{3}{3}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{4}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-\\frac{∇f(3,3,3)}{‖∇f(3,3,3)‖} \\\\ & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{(\\frac{4}{3})^{2}+(\\frac{1}{3})^{2}+(1)^{2}}}⟨\\frac{4}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,1⟩ \\\\ & =⟨-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{26}}{13},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{26},\\,-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{26}}{26}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function decreases most rapidly in the unit direction of $⟨-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{26}}{13},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{26}}{26},\\,-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{26}}{26}⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["13f6643a-75d9-50a2-a3fb-88100e3589a1"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "8b93f0c7-7cb1-5c58-98b0-702b47f27086" :answer/id #uuid "8b93f0c7-7cb1-5c58-98b0-702b47f27086" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4d2355f9-7bdf-5219-b0ed-8b759d10a82f" :answer/id #uuid "4d2355f9-7bdf-5219-b0ed-8b759d10a82f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e026aebe-c32c-5814-a5e2-37e617185f18" :answer/id #uuid "e026aebe-c32c-5814-a5e2-37e617185f18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9d62897b-0837-5ff3-bf6a-1d842243f83d" :answer/id #uuid "9d62897b-0837-5ff3-bf6a-1d842243f83d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{33}}{33},\\,-\\frac{4 \\sqrt{33}}{33},\\,-\\frac{4 \\sqrt{33}}{33}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4510612c-f80f-5c67-8138-7e4b58f04da5" :answer/id #uuid "4510612c-f80f-5c67-8138-7e4b58f04da5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{3}{17},\\,-\\frac{2}{17},\\,-\\frac{2}{17}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "dc0ce43d-cf21-522b-b594-14d9ac1ad0d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc0ce43d-cf21-522b-b594-14d9ac1ad0d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["8b93f0c7-7cb1-5c58-98b0-702b47f27086" "4d2355f9-7bdf-5219-b0ed-8b759d10a82f" "e026aebe-c32c-5814-a5e2-37e617185f18" "9d62897b-0837-5ff3-bf6a-1d842243f83d" "4510612c-f80f-5c67-8138-7e4b58f04da5"] :answer-field/correct "8b93f0c7-7cb1-5c58-98b0-702b47f27086" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "aaff19d2-1089-5ffb-bb3e-92011188d5ba" :question/id #uuid "aaff19d2-1089-5ffb-bb3e-92011188d5ba" :question/problem "In what unit direction does the function $f(x,y,z)=\\ln (x^{6}y^{4}z^{4})$ decrease most rapidly at the point $(2,2,2)$?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ decreases most rapidly in the direction opposite to that of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(2,2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (x^{6}y^{4}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln (x^{6}y^{4}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\ln (x^{6}y^{4}z^{4}))⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{1}{x^{6}y^{4}z^{4}}\\cdot 6x^{5}y^{4}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{6}y^{4}z^{4}}\\cdot 4x^{6}y^{3}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{6}y^{4}z^{4}}\\cdot 4x^{6}y^{4}z^{3}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{6}{x},\\,\\frac{4}{y},\\,\\frac{4}{z}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(2,2,2) & =⟨\\frac{6}{2},\\,\\frac{4}{2},\\,\\frac{4}{2}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨3,\\,2,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =-\\frac{∇f(2,2,2)}{‖∇f(2,2,2)‖} \\\\ & =\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(2)^{2}}}⟨3,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\ & =⟨-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function decreases most rapidly in the unit direction of $⟨-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17},\\,-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{17}}{17}⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["dc0ce43d-cf21-522b-b594-14d9ac1ad0d8"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "24903325-fc0a-5ecb-8f57-b0303e5a47b8" :answer/id #uuid "24903325-fc0a-5ecb-8f57-b0303e5a47b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{15}{43},\\,\\frac{9}{43},\\,\\frac{9}{43}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8b2f65ba-0cc3-5296-bb1b-f4544ca841ad" :answer/id #uuid "8b2f65ba-0cc3-5296-bb1b-f4544ca841ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{3},\\,1,\\,1⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "568e7e09-9ada-5d4d-832e-c907e2ae3641" :answer/id #uuid "568e7e09-9ada-5d4d-832e-c907e2ae3641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{19},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{19}}{19},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{19}}{19}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "58d7dd0e-16b3-5cb7-ae74-c242f146528e" :answer/id #uuid "58d7dd0e-16b3-5cb7-ae74-c242f146528e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1be8f1ac-37b5-58a3-955f-0739f5c4af3a" :answer/id #uuid "1be8f1ac-37b5-58a3-955f-0739f5c4af3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{5 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,-\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43}⟩" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8c843ff1-9a50-5ae1-8952-8cb69c4ce0ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c843ff1-9a50-5ae1-8952-8cb69c4ce0ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["24903325-fc0a-5ecb-8f57-b0303e5a47b8" "8b2f65ba-0cc3-5296-bb1b-f4544ca841ad" "568e7e09-9ada-5d4d-832e-c907e2ae3641" "58d7dd0e-16b3-5cb7-ae74-c242f146528e" "1be8f1ac-37b5-58a3-955f-0739f5c4af3a"] :answer-field/correct "58d7dd0e-16b3-5cb7-ae74-c242f146528e" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "d24d013a-ecfd-5200-be0e-2480338379cf" :question/id #uuid "d24d013a-ecfd-5200-be0e-2480338379cf" :question/problem "In what unit direction does the function $f(x,y,z)=\\ln (x^{5}y^{2}z^{2})$ increase most rapidly at the point $(3,2,2)$?" :question/worked-solution "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $∇f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(3,2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\ln (x^{5}y^{2}z^{2})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\ln (x^{5}y^{2}z^{2})),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\ln (x^{5}y^{2}z^{2}))⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{1}{x^{5}y^{2}z^{2}}\\cdot 5x^{4}y^{2}z^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{5}y^{2}z^{2}}\\cdot 2x^{5}y^{1}z^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{5}y^{2}z^{2}}\\cdot 2x^{5}y^{2}z^{1}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{5}{x},\\,\\frac{2}{y},\\,\\frac{2}{z}⟩ \\\\ ∇f(3,2,2) & =⟨\\frac{5}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{2},\\,\\frac{2}{2}⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{5}{3},\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{∇f(3,2,2)}{‖∇f(3,2,2)‖} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(\\frac{5}{3})^{2}+(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}}}⟨\\frac{5}{3},\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ & =⟨\\frac{5 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the unit direction of $⟨\\frac{5 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43},\\,\\frac{3 \\sqrt{43}}{43}⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["8c843ff1-9a50-5ae1-8952-8cb69c4ce0ca"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "571dc50a-1c8e-5ef3-85a4-84e5e40856c5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186124459.py"} [:db/add 17592186124459 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186124459 :knowledge-point/questions ["48a5b0a5-ecb9-5e4e-bbb7-138d96fc81cd" "a6e0bfcc-2db2-5134-b63f-ed16edd03447" "6d226b9a-26b3-5e84-bd16-a03937995368" "b1292b8d-2b01-5533-896d-f2505b0485b1" "aaff19d2-1089-5ffb-bb3e-92011188d5ba" "d24d013a-ecfd-5200-be0e-2480338379cf"]} [:db/ensure 17592186124459 :knowledge-point/validate]]
